.env
.env.*
!.env.example
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
packages/*/node_modules/
packages/contracts/cache/
packages/contracts/out/
packages/contracts/broadcast/
packages/contracts/.openzeppelin/
packages/contracts/deployments/*.local.json
coverage/
dist/
# EXCEPTION: @nuvem/contracts-artifacts/dist is the one build product that must
# be tracked. It is the only way the web container can get the ABIs -- Foundry
# is not installed there, and the export script's --skip-forge path still reads
# packages/contracts/out/ (gitignored, line 8). Railway builds from git, so
# there is nowhere to inject a host-built directory from.
# Order matters: git will not descend into an excluded directory, so the
# directory must be re-included before its contents.
!packages/contracts-artifacts/dist/
!packages/contracts-artifacts/dist/**
*.log

# @nuvem/keeper: signing-key material and the durable settled-window ledger.
# secrets/ is where docker-compose.yml's keeper service expects a mounted
# attester key file to live (docs/runbooks/ATTESTER.md). state/ is the
# append-only journal of every settlement the keeper has made -- it is
# correctness-critical for ONE deployment and actively misleading in any other,
# so it belongs on a volume and in a backup, never in git.
#
# BOTH NAMES MATTER. `state/` is what docker-compose.yml and the runbook mount.
# `.keeper-state/` is the DEFAULT in src/config.ts when NUVEM_KEEPER_STATE_DIR is
# unset, which is exactly what `pnpm --dir packages/keeper-old tick` on a laptop
# produces -- and it was the one not ignored, so the journal of a real operator's
# realized trading profits sat untracked-but-committable, one `git add -A` from a
# public commit. The bare `.keeper-state/` is here too because the keeper creates
# that directory relative to whatever cwd it was started from, which is not always
# packages/keeper-old. There is deliberately no bare `state/` rule: it is a common
# enough directory name that it would silently swallow real source one day.
secrets/
packages/keeper-old/state/
packages/keeper-old/.keeper-state/
.keeper-state/

# Vendored agent-skill content. Regenerable from skills-lock.json with
# `npx skills add`, so the lockfile is tracked and the payload is not.
.agents/
.claude/skills/

# Working state for scripts/testnet-drill.sh. It records what a drill built so
# the script can refuse to run a step twice — which means a committed copy makes
# a fresh clone believe a deployment already happened. The addresses that matter
# live in reports/, which is a record rather than a lock.
packages/contracts/.drill-state/

# The sealed env bundle. scripts/secrets-bundle.sh can still make one, but SIP
# does not carry it in git: Nuvem's held five Safe owner keys, and publishing
# ciphertext only buys time against an offline attacker.
secrets.enc

# Nuvem's brand media (91 MB of video and a 33 MB background) — the SIP site
# serves none of it. Kept out so a clone stays a few megabytes.
images-assets/
packages/website-oficial/public/brand/

# Finder droppings and a stray boot log from the old stack.
.DS_Store
.nuvem-logs-boot.txt

# Next.js build output, wherever it lands (a stray `next build` from the repo root makes one here).
.next/

# Brand source art: multi-megabyte, full-resolution originals. The site ships the
# derived cut-outs in public/logo/ and src/app/, which are a few KB each.
packages/website-oficial/brand-source/
